<title>USA: IBM slips to 101 after hours, volume light.</title>
<headline>IBM slips to 101 after hours, volume light.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of International Business Machines Corp receded to 101 in after-hours trading on Monday, down from an unofficial close of 103-11/16, a trader said.</p>
<p>The dealer stressed that the activity was very light by the time a halt in trading IBM shares ended late in the after-hours session. The trade involved only 1,000 shares.</p>
<p>Bellwether IBM posted second-quarter earnings of $1.46 per share after the U.S. market close, compared with a First Call consensus estimate of $1.42.</p>
